# Generate, Rerank, and Create Menu
# This script first generates a large dataset of dishes using a generative model,
# then uses the reranker to extract specific dish types, and finally creates a menu.

# Step 1: Generate the dataset of 60 dishes (20 from each country)
/model mistral_1
/clearfile
/multiline
Please list 20 popular traditional dishes from France, 20 from Germany, and 20 from Spain (60 dishes in total). 
Format the output as a simple list with one dish per line, including a brief description of its ingredients. 
Ensure the list includes a variety of items, specifically desserts, chicken dishes, and vegetable dishes.
;;
/multiline
/save 60_generated_dishes.txt

# Step 2: Set up the document source for reranking
# We load the newly generated text file into a filebank and set it as the target
/filebank1 60_generated_dishes.txt
/documents filebank=1

# Step 3: Extract the specific dishes using semantic search
# Switch to the reranker model
/model nvidia_reranker

# Extract a vegetable dish
/rerank "traditional vegetable dish or vegetarian stew" top_n=1 split=line items=1 return=text
/setvar menu_vegetable {LAST_RESPONSE}

# Extract a chicken dish
/rerank "traditional chicken poultry dish" top_n=1 split=line items=1 return=text
/setvar menu_chicken {LAST_RESPONSE}

# Extract a dessert
/rerank "sweet dessert cake pastry" top_n=1 split=line items=1 return=text
/setvar menu_dessert {LAST_RESPONSE}

# Step 4: Create the final menu
# Switch back to the generative model
/model mistral_1
/clearfile
/multiline
You are the head chef of a prestigious European restaurant. 
I have selected the following three dishes from our expansive culinary database:

Appetizer (Vegetable):
${menu_vegetable}

Main Course (Chicken):
${menu_chicken}

Dessert:
${menu_dessert}

Please write a highly elegant and creative menu description for this 3-course meal. Describe how the flavors progress from the appetizer to the main course and finish with the dessert.
;;
/multiline

# Save the final output
/save generated_3_course_menu.txt
